The items excavated during the 1938 excavation (13th year of the Showa era) are as follows{{Sfn|塚の腰古墳・松面古墳発掘調査報告書|2016}}. The manual excavation items were purchased and preserved by the {{ill|Tokyo National Museum|ja|東京国立博物館|12=draft}} through Kisarazu Police and Chiba Prefecture, while the items unearthed by the survey team were transferred to and preserved at {{ill|Kokugakuin University|ja|國學院大學|12=draft}}; the collections at both the Tokyo National Museum and the Kokugakuin University Museum are labeled with T and K respectively{{Sfn|塚の腰古墳・松面古墳発掘調査報告書|2016}}.
* Decorated Sword
** Bronze‐adorned Double Dragon Ring‐Headed Sword, 1 (T)
** Bronze‐adorned Sword, 1 (location unknown)
** Silver‐adorned Twisted Ring‐Headed Sword Hilt, 1 (T)
** Bronze‐made Sword Scabbard Ornament Fragment, collectively (T)
** Skull‐shaped Sword Hilt, 1 (location unknown)
* Weapons
** Straight Sword, 2 or more (T) – possibly the blade portion of the bronze scabbard ornament fragment
** Iron halberd shaft and stone tip (K)
** Silver‐made dagger (possibly K)
** Iron arrowheads (T, K)
* Ornaments
** Bronze‐made Double Fish‐shaped Pendant, 1 pair (T)
** Bronze‐made Glass Bead‐attached Leaf‐shaped Waist Ornament, 1 pair (K)
** Bronze‐made Square Floral‐shaped Ornaments, 9 (K)
** Small glass beads – possibly from the leaf‐shaped waist ornament
* Horse Fittings
** Bronze‐made Heart‐shaped Apricot Leaf with hinge, 2 (T)
** Bronze‐adorned saddle and stirrup fittings, 3 sets (T1, K2)
** Bronze‐made remnants of a covered wheel, 6 (T)
** Incomplete iron spurred stirrup, 1 pair (T)
** Iron‐based bronze leather fastening fittings, 6 (T)
* Bronze bowl, 1 (K)
* {{ill|Sue pottery|ja|須恵器|1=Sue pottery|12=draft}} – 3 broken lids, 3 or more broken bodies; 5 high broken jars with lids, 4 high broken jars with lids, 2 high broken jars without lids, 2 long‐necked jars with feet, 1 long‐necked jar with lid, 1 footed crucible, 1 jar (all T)
* {{ill|Haji pottery|ja|土師器|1=Haji pottery|12=draft}} – 1 broken vessel, 3 jars (all T)

